1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,950
Welcome to The Efficiency Edge.

2
00:00:01,950 --> 00:00:03,005
I'm Phil.

3
00:00:03,088 --> 00:00:03,483
Today,

4
00:00:03,483 --> 00:00:05,283
we're decoding the money story behind

5
00:00:05,283 --> 00:00:06,616
the headlines.

6
00:00:07,150 --> 00:00:08,996
When Nvidia's CEO quit,

7
00:00:08,996 --> 00:00:10,215
the stock fell as much as

8
00:00:10,215 --> 00:00:12,489
fourteen percent in a single day.

9
00:00:12,630 --> 00:00:14,116
When the board brought him back,

10
00:00:14,116 --> 00:00:16,378
it closed thirty-one percent higher.

11
00:00:16,589 --> 00:00:18,644
A company worth trillions of dollars,

12
00:00:18,644 --> 00:00:20,302
swinging on one man.

13
00:00:20,699 --> 00:00:21,431
The next day,

14
00:00:21,431 --> 00:00:22,743
it slipped six percent,

15
00:00:22,743 --> 00:00:24,540
as the excitement faded.

16
00:00:24,937 --> 00:00:26,760
Here's what that tells you: this

17
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:28,791
market isn't just betting on AI.

18
00:00:28,791 --> 00:00:30,010
It's betting on a handful of

19
00:00:30,010 --> 00:00:30,833
people.

20
00:00:30,974 --> 00:00:32,147
So what happens when one of

21
00:00:32,147 --> 00:00:33,921
them walks away for good?

